th='Courage, duty and supreme sacrifice for the nation – the first Param Vir Chakra.',
sum='Major Somnath Sharma was India’s first recipient of the Param Vir Chakra. In August 1947 Pakistan launched Operation Gulmarg to annex the Kashmir Valley, breaking its agreement with Maharaja Hari Singh. About 1000 trained invaders entered Kashmir on 22 October 1947 to capture strategic places, including Srinagar airport; Kashmir joined India on 26 October and Indian troops were airlifted on 27 October. On 31 October, D Company of 4 Kumaon under Major Somnath Sharma was flown in; his left hand was in plaster, but he insisted, “I know my men better than anyone else… they are not going in without me.” On 3 November 1947, at Badgam (less than 5 km from the airport), about 500 infiltrators attacked his 90 men. He guessed the first attack was a distraction, requested air strikes and bravely laid out ground panels to guide the aircraft. Outnumbered seven to one, he moved fearlessly, directed fire, filled magazines for his gunners and encouraged his men. When ammunition ran low and he was asked to pull back, he said, “The enemy is only 50 yards from us… I shall not withdraw an inch but will fight to the last man and the last round.” Minutes later a mortar shell killed him. Inspired by him, his men held their position for six more hours, giving time for reinforcements to arrive and causing over 300 enemy casualties – Srinagar was saved. He died at 24 and was awarded the PVC posthumously. Born on 31 January 1923 at Dadh, Kangra (Himachal Pradesh), son of Major General Amar Nath Sharma, inspired by Mahabharata tales told by his grandfather, he studied at Sherwood College, Nainital and Sandhurst, was commissioned in 1942 and earned mention in despatches in Burma (World War II). His name is on the Honour Wall of the National War Memorial.',
te='మేజర్ సోమనాథ్ శర్మ – మొదటి పరమవీర చక్ర గ్రహీత. 1947లో పాకిస్తాన్ “ఆపరేషన్ గుల్మార్గ్” ద్వారా కాశ్మీర్ ఆక్రమణకు చొరబాటుదారులను పంపింది. 3 నవంబర్ 1947న బద్గామ్‌లో ఆయన నాయకత్వంలోని D కంపెనీ 90 మంది సుమారు 500 మంది చొరబాటుదారులను ఎదుర్కొన్నారు. చేయికి కట్టు ఉన్నా ఆయన వైమానిక దాడులకు గుర్తులు పెట్టి, తుపాకులకు మ్యాగజైన్లు నింపుతూ సైనికులను ప్రోత్సహించారు. “ఒక్క అంగుళం కూడా వెనక్కి తగ్గను, చివరి మనిషి, చివరి తూటా వరకు పోరాడతాను” అన్నారు. మోర్టార్ షెల్ తగిలి వీరమరణం పొందారు. ఆయన సైనికులు ఆరు గంటలు నిలిచి శ్రీనగర్ విమానాశ్రయాన్ని కాపాడారు. 24 ఏళ్లకే దేశం కోసం ప్రాణాలర్పించిన ఆయనకు మరణానంతరం పరమవీర చక్ర లభించింది.',
